3f:["$","$L5d",null,{"type":"multiple","children":[["$","$L5e",null,{"title":"Can clients other than Bazel use this?","id":"can-clients-other-than-bazel-use-this","children":["$","p",null,{"children":["Yes: the config exposes standard Remote Execution API services, so Buck2,\nPants, Siso, and recc point at ",["$","code",null,{"children":"127.0.0.1:50051"}]," the same way. The Bazel\nflags are just the worked example;\n",["$","$L1b",null,{"href":"/getting-started/connect-your-build","children":"Connect your build"}]," has the others."]}]}],["$","$L5e",null,{"title":"Is a local cluster a reasonable everyday setup?","id":"is-a-local-cluster-a-reasonable-everyday-setup","children":["$","p",null,{"children":["For sandboxed, cached single-machine builds, yes. What it can't give you is\nparallelism beyond one worker's ",["$","code",null,{"children":"cpu_count"}],", or sharing with anyone else.\nThe moment you want either, you want a real deployment:\n",["$","$L1b",null,{"href":"/operate/production-config","children":"Production configuration"}],"."]}]}],["$","$L5e",null,{"title":"Should I test config changes here before deploying them?","id":"should-i-test-config-changes-here-before-deploying","children":["$","p",null,{"children":"Yes, and it's the main reason to keep a local cluster around. Store\ncomposition, scheduler property maps, and service wiring all fail the same\nway locally as they do in a cluster, and the feedback loop is seconds\ninstead of a deploy."}]}]]}]
